    "result_text": "The only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest` (the other files in that package are base/helper classes). The full suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` derived field so that it returns `'EMAIL'` when an email is present and `'PHONE'` otherwise, following the existing conventions for derived owner fields (like `membershipLevel` and `locality`):\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a deterministic static helper `contactPreference(String email)` returning `\"EMAIL\"` when a non-empty email is present, else `\"PHONE\"`.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (kept it a plain string, matching the `locality` pattern, to avoid enum-type friction in the MapStruct mapper).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Mapped `contactPreference` via a `formatContactPreference(owner)` expression delegating to `Owner.contactPreference(owner.getEmail())`, mirroring the other derived-field mappings.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
