    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the codebase's established pattern exactly. There is a clear, repeated idiom here: each derived DTO field has (1) a pure `static` derivation method on `Owner` (`householdId`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`) and (2) a thin `formatXxx` default method in `OwnerMapper` that null-guards the owner and delegates to that static method, wired via `@Mapping(... expression = ...)`. \n\nThe new `Owner.contactPreference(String email)` and `OwnerMapper.formatContactPreference(Owner)` slot into this structure precisely:\n- Derivation logic lives on the domain model alongside its siblings (`locality`, `membershipLevel`), which is the right unit \u2014 it's a deterministic function of a persisted field, and `membershipLevel` already derives from `email` the same way.\n- The mapper method is a consistent null-guarding delegator, matching the others in placement, Javadoc style (including the `see {@link ...}` cross-reference), and ordering (placed next to `formatBulkSignupWarning`, just before `toOwner`).\n- No duplication, no new catch-all; the OpenAPI schema addition mirrors the other derived read-only fields.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this entirely natural.",
